From 7493dd6f85e15c6d539e2e41985212844e86452c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:52:07 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 017/152] mfd: sec: Add read-only S2MPS18 support over ACPM

Add the S2MPS18 PMIC found on Exynos9810 boards. Like the S2MPG1x, it is
reached through ACPM IPC (channel 2, the "acpm-ipc-channel" of the stock
s2mps18mfd node). The ACPM PMIC command layout is unchanged: register
in bits [7:0] and block type in [11:8] of word 0 with TOP = 0, PMIC = 1
and RTC = 2 (downstream drivers/mfd/s2mps18_core.c I2C_ADDR_*), and
function/value/mask/return in word 1 (downstream acpm_mfd.h).

For bring-up the device is strictly read-only: the regmaps have no
writeable registers and the bus callbacks refuse writes and updates, so
nothing on the PMIC can be changed while the firmware keeps scaling the
DVFS rails. As a consequence, interrupts (which need mask writes) and
the RTC are left out, and the IRQ is not requested. The PMIC ID from
the TOP block is logged at probe as a first sign of life.

There is no power meter regmap yet, so make it optional, and skip the
wake IRQ handling in suspend/resume when there is no IRQ.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
